{"created": "2024-03-15T15:09:38.368401+00:00", "modified": "2025-06-28T17:41:07.129286+00:00", "id": 10822316, "conceptrecid": "10174170", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.10822316", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.10174170", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10822316", "metadata": {"title": "Standard Solar Models B23 / SF-III", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.10822316", "publication_date": "2023-11-21", "description": "<p>This package contains data from a variety of up-to-date Solar Models as well as a routine to generate variations of them in a Linear Solar Model (LSM) approximation. The provided data includes the solar inner structure for several physical variables and abundances for chemical species of interest, as well as neutrino outflows and distributions from different sources and their correlation matrices.</p>\n<p>The available Solar Models differ in the proposed solar composition, and were all computed with a modified version of <em>GarStEC</em>, using the latest prescription for nuclear reaction rates and opacity data from the upcoming <em><strong>Solar Fusion III</strong></em> review article by Acharya et al. (submitted: <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.06470\">arXiv:2405.06470</a>), and references therein. The proposed solar compositions are (in chronological order):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\"GS98\" &nbsp; &nbsp; :: Grevesse &amp; Sauval (1998), Space Sci. Rev., 85, 161.</li>\n<li>\"AGSS09\" :: Asplund et al. (2009), ARA&amp;A, 47, 481.</li>\n<li>\"C11\" &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;:: Caffau et al. (2011), Sol. Phys., 268, 255.</li>\n<li>\"AAG21\" &nbsp; :: Asplund et al. (2021), A&amp;A 653, A141.</li>\n<li>\"MB22m\" &nbsp;:: Magg et al. (2022), A&amp;A 661, A140. (Meteoritic)</li>\n<li>\"MB22p\" &nbsp; :: Magg et al. (2022), A&amp;A 661, A140. (Photospheric)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;See the ReadMe file included in the package for a detailed list of content.</p>\n<p>Developed by Y. Herrera , and A. Serenelli ,<br>Institute of Space Sciences (ICE - CSIC), Barcelona, Spain.<br>This package is made available as part of the ChETEC-INFRA collaboration.&nbsp;</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Herrera, Yago", "affiliation": "Institute of Space Sciences", "orcid": "0000-0002-6469-1942"}, {"name": "Serenelli, Aldo", "affiliation": "Institute of Space Sciences", "orcid": "0000-0001-6359-2769"}], "keywords": ["solar models", "nuclear rates", "solar composition", "helioseismology"], "version": "v1.2", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "grants": [{"code": "101008324", "internal_id": "10.13039/501100000780::101008324", "funder": {"name": "European Commission", "doi": "10.13039/501100000780", "acronym": "EC"}, "title": "Chemical Elements as Tracers of the Evolution of the Cosmos - Infrastructures for Nuclear Astrophysics", "acronym": "ChETEC-INFRA", "program": "H2020-EU.1.4.", "url": "https://cordis.europa.eu/projects/101008324"}], "communities": [{"id": "chetec-infra-wp8"}, {"id": "eu"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "10174170"}}]}}, "title": "Standard Solar Models B23 / SF-III", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10822316", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/10822316", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/10822316?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10822316", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10822316", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.10822316", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10822316/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10174170", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/10174170", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10174170", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.10174170", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:10822316/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:10822316/sequence/default"